## Session interface handoff

- `useGameSession()` in `src/game/session/useGameSession.ts` returns
  `game`, `dealId`, `paused`, `best`, `celebrating`, `status`,
  `announcement: {serial, text}`, and methods `activateCard(index)`,
  `newGame()`, `restart()`, `changeSize(size)`, `loadBoard(draft)`,
  `loadSnapshot(draft)`, `exportSnapshot()`, and `resume()`.
- `dealId` increments only for a new deal, restart, size change, or successful
  board/snapshot import. Card and clock updates leave it alone, so UI drafts and
  remembered board focus can remain stable through ordinary play.
- `status` carries the visible reproduction-control result; each turn/load
  announcement increments its independent `serial`, even for repeated identical
  text. The UI owns the single atomic polite live region.
- `resume()` removes the pause; its click handler should focus the board's
  remembered card before calling it because the Resume button disappears.
- Session time uses an injected monotonic clock. The mismatch deadline runs
  against remaining active time and is canceled on hide, pause, deal replacement,
  and cleanup. Timer callbacks check generations and deal identity.
